  [1m[38;5;153mindex.html[39m (modified).[0m One line: [38;5;153m<script src="session.js"></script>[39m before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, since [38;5;153mapp.js[39m constructs the session
  at load.

  [1mOut of scope, flagged not silently built:[0m there is no logout control anywhere in this app. The design gives you
  [38;5;153mclear()[39m, but wiring a logout button is a UI change you didn't ask for. Without it, the stored identity persists until
  the browser's storage is cleared by hand — worth knowing, given you chose [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m.

  Alongside this: the repo has no linter, formatter, test runner, or CI. Tooling is cheapest to add before the code
  exists, and approach C already brings a test runner. My recommendation is [38;5;153mnode:test[39m (built into Node, zero
  dependencies, consistent with the repo having no [38;5;153mdevDependencies[39m) plus Biome or Prettier for formatting only if you
  want it — I wouldn't add more than that to a four-file project.

